/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] for [`crate::version::BumpLevel`] in a
/// follow-up commit, matching the [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::OsStr>`]
/// OS-string borrowed-view parse opening order (d37e6fe → 9fca3bb →
/// 1ea7110) at the OS-string sibling, the [`TryFrom<&[u8]>`] byte-slice
/// borrowed-view parse opening order (5c0c827 → cdb192c → 629b242) at
/// the byte-slice sibling, and the [`From<T> for std::ffi::CString`]
/// C-string owned emit opening order (020317a → 1e8ed3c → 6cff423) at
/// this C-string frontier's emit-side dual.
///
/// # Two-stage strictness
///
/// The parser is strict at the same TWO frontiers a direct
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] + [`str::parse`] composition would be
/// strict at, lifted to ONE typed-primitive site:
///
/// - Non-UTF-8 byte sequences (a [`&std::ffi::CStr`] carries any byte
///   sequence excluding interior NUL — a `getenv(3)` return under a
///   non-UTF-8 locale, a C-emitted log frame under a foreign character
///   set, a raw `*const c_char` handed back by a legacy C library)
///   reject at the [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] Unicode-decode frontier
///   with a diagnostic naming the offending C-string.
/// - Valid-UTF-8 C-string sequences that decode to a non-canonical
///   label (`b"Refused\0"`, `b"StagingOnly\0"`, `b"Strict\0"`,
///   `b"REFUSED\0"`, `b" refused\0"`, `b"refused \0"`,
///   `b"stagingonly\0"`, `b"\0"` the empty NUL-terminated C-string)
///   reject at the underlying [`std::str::FromStr`] impl — the same
///   canonical-only strictness the UTF-8, byte-slice, and OS-string
///   frontiers already carry at the by-reference parse peers, now
///   lifted to the NUL-terminated C-string input layer at ONE
///   composition through the borrowed [`TryFrom<&str>`] peer.
///
/// The identity `AdmissionTier::try_from(<&std::ffi::CStr>::from(
/// canonical_cstring_bytes(tier))).unwrap() == tier` at every
/// [`AdmissionTier::ALL`] variant is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstr_agrees_with_from_str`];
/// the identity carried through a generic
/// `impl for<'a> TryFrom<&'a std::ffi::CStr>` consumer at every variant
/// is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstr_carries_through_generic_consumer`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on non-UTF-8 NUL-terminated C-string
/// input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstr_rejects_non_utf8_input`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on valid-UTF-8 non-canonical
/// NUL-terminated C-string input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstr_rejects_non_canonical_input`].
///
/// THEORY.md §V.4 typed primitives: the by-reference NUL-terminated
/// C-string parse surface is a typed-primitive site on
/// [`AdmissionTier`] itself (one `TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>` impl
/// routing through [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] and the by-reference
/// [`TryFrom<&str>`] parse peer), not a per-consumer
/// `AdmissionTier::try_from(c.to_str().map_err(...)?)` restatement at
/// every downstream site that types its parse contract as
/// `impl for<'a> TryFrom<&'a std::ffi::CStr>`.
/// THEORY.md §VI.1 one-oracle: the canonical label grammar is named at
/// one site ([`AdmissionTier::as_str`]), inverted at one site
/// ([`<AdmissionTier as std::str::FromStr>::from_str`]), and every
/// parse surface — [`std::str::FromStr`], [`serde::Deserialize`],
/// [`TryFrom<&str>`], [`TryFrom<String>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, str>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<str>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&[u8]>`], [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, [u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<[u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::OsStr>`], [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::path::Path>`], [`TryFrom<std::path::PathBuf>`], and
/// this [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] — reads through it.
impl TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr> for AdmissionTier {
    type Error = anyhow::Error;

    fn try_from(c: &std::ffi::CStr) -> Result<Self, Self::Error> {
        let decoded = c.to_str().map_err(|e| {
            anyhow::anyhow!("invalid UTF-8 in admission tier CStr input {c:?}: {e}")
        })?;
        <Self as std::convert::TryFrom<&str>>::try_from(decoded)
    }
}

/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString> for AdmissionTier`] routes through the
/// by-reference [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] parse peer directly above on
/// [`std::ffi::CString::as_c_str`] of the caller-owned NUL-terminated
/// C-string buffer, so a downstream consumer bound by
/// `impl TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>` (a `serde` container that opts into
/// `#[serde(try_from = "CString")]` on a wrapper field, a generic
/// try-conversion helper `fn parse_c_field<T: TryFrom<CString>>` that owns
/// the input NUL-terminated C-string, a validated-input newtype builder
/// that consumes an owned [`std::ffi::CString`] and returns a validated
/// [`AdmissionTier`], a [`std::ffi::CString::from_vec_with_nul`] receiver
/// that owns the returned [`std::ffi::CString`] over a FFI-produced
/// buffer, a [`std::ffi::CString::new`] terminus that owns the
/// freshly-allocated NUL-terminated buffer, a `libc::getenv` +
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr`] + [`std::ffi::CStr::to_owned`] compose
/// that owns the process-environment slot's NUL-terminated payload)
/// recovers an [`AdmissionTier`] value from a canonical snake_case-label
/// owned NUL-terminated C-string through the same one-oracle grammar the
/// direct `.parse::<AdmissionTier>()` call sites, the sibling
/// [`TryFrom<&str>`], [`TryFrom<String>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, str>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<str>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&[u8]>`], [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, [u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<[u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::OsStr>`], [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::path::Path>`], [`TryFrom<std::path::PathBuf>`], and
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] parse peers already read.
///
/// The by-value owned-buffer NUL-terminated C-string parse peer of
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr> for AdmissionTier`] directly above — both
/// are parse surfaces of the NUL-terminated C-string frontier, differing
/// only on the input C-string ownership: [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`]
/// takes a borrowed [`&std::ffi::CStr`] view for consumers that already
/// hold a borrow (a `*const c_char` FFI return surfaced through
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr`], a `getenv(3)` reader that keeps the
/// process-environment slot borrowed, a `syslog(3)` / `journald` bridge
/// that reads a canonical NUL-terminated label off a C-emitted log frame
/// without allocating), this [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] takes an
/// owned [`std::ffi::CString`] for consumers that own the input
/// NUL-terminated C-string buffer (a `serde` `try_from = "CString"`
/// container, a C-string-consuming builder, a [`std::ffi::CString::new`]
/// receiver, a [`std::ffi::CString::from_vec_with_nul`] receiver). Both
/// delegate through the shared [`FromStr`] parse oracle: the borrowed
/// peer through [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] + [`TryFrom<&str>`] (which
/// itself composes through [`FromStr`]), this owned peer through the
/// borrowed peer via [`std::ffi::CString::as_c_str`] at the boundary —
/// the same canonical grammar lifted to the owned-buffer input layer.
///
/// Structural mirror of [`TryFrom<String> for AdmissionTier`] at the
/// UTF-8 frontier, [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>> for AdmissionTier`] at the
/// byte-slice frontier, and [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString> for
/// AdmissionTier`] at the OS-string frontier — the same by-value
/// owned-input parse surface at the same one-oracle discipline, projected
/// onto the NUL-terminated C-string frontier.
///
/// Mid-trio peer of the by-value owned-buffer NUL-terminated C-string
/// parse trio at the admission-tier ladder:
/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] for [`crate::retry::PerAttemptRegion`]
/// (commit e73daa7) opened the trio at the first ordered typed sum; the
/// closing peer at the third ordered typed sum is
/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] for [`crate::version::BumpLevel`] in a
/// follow-up commit, matching the [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`]
/// borrowed-view parse opening order (8777e9f → 95ddf71 → 5073623) at the
/// borrowed-view counterpart, the [`TryFrom<String>`] UTF-8 owned-input
/// parse opening order at the UTF-8 frontier's owned-input counterpart,
/// the [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>>`] byte-slice owned-input parse opening order at
/// the byte-slice frontier's owned-input counterpart, the
/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString>`] OS-string owned-input parse opening
/// order at the OS-string frontier's owned-input counterpart, and the
/// [`From<AdmissionTier> for std::ffi::CString`] owned-emit opening order
/// (020317a → 1e8ed3c → 6cff423) at the NUL-terminated C-string
/// frontier's emit-side owned-buffer dual.
///
/// The natural bridge to any downstream site that types its
/// NUL-terminated C-string parse contract as
/// `impl TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>` rather than
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] — the NUL-terminated C-string frontier's
/// `serde` `try_from` container attribute at the owned-buffer layer
/// (`#[serde(try_from = "CString")]` — which keys off
/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`], not [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`]), a
/// validated-input newtype builder whose canonical parse contract is
/// stated as `TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>` (consumes the caller's input
/// NUL-terminated C-string end-to-end), a
/// [`std::ffi::CString::from_vec_with_nul`] terminus that owns the
/// returned [`std::ffi::CString`] and hands it to a typed parser without
/// a borrow-then-clone round trip. The [`FromStr`] impl carries the
/// load-bearing match body against the canonical grammar; this
/// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] impl delegates through the
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] parse peer (which itself composes
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] with [`TryFrom<&str>`] which composes
/// [`FromStr`]), so the parse-oracle discipline is preserved end-to-end
/// and a future variant insertion / grammar refinement remains a
/// one-site edit at [`AdmissionTier::as_str`] plus the matching
/// [`FromStr`] arm addition.
///
/// # Two-stage strictness
///
/// The parser is strict at the same TWO frontiers the
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] peer directly above is strict at,
/// inherited through the delegation: non-UTF-8 NUL-terminated C-string
/// byte sequences reject at [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] with the standard
/// "invalid UTF-8 in admission tier CStr input" diagnostic surfaced
/// through [`anyhow::Error`], and valid-UTF-8 NUL-terminated C-string
/// sequences that decode to a non-canonical label (`""`, `"Refused"`,
/// `"StagingOnly"`, `"Strict"`, `"REFUSED"`, `" refused"`, `"refused "`,
/// `"stagingonly"`) reject at the underlying [`FromStr`] impl — the same
/// canonical-only strictness the NUL-terminated C-string frontier
/// already carries at the by-reference peer, now lifted to the
/// owned-buffer input layer at ONE composition through the borrowed
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] peer.
///
/// The impl body picks [`std::ffi::CString::as_c_str`] rather than
/// [`std::ffi::CString::into_string`] or an intermediate `to_str` +
/// [`str::parse`] restatement: [`std::ffi::CString::as_c_str`] yields a
/// borrowed [`&std::ffi::CStr`] view of the caller-owned buffer without
/// allocation, so the parse-side receiver pays the by-reference
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] cost, not the [`String`]-allocation cost
/// of a [`std::ffi::CString::into_string`] round trip. The owned
/// [`std::ffi::CString`] input is dropped at return, freeing its buffer
/// exactly once — the same discipline the sibling [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<String>`], and [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString>`] owned-buffer
/// parse peers apply at the [`Vec::as_slice`], [`String::as_str`], and
/// [`std::ffi::OsString::as_os_str`] boundaries at the byte-slice,
/// UTF-8, and OS-string frontiers.
///
/// The identity `AdmissionTier::try_from(std::ffi::CString::new(
/// tier.as_str()).unwrap()).unwrap() == tier` at every
/// [`AdmissionTier::ALL`] variant is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstring_agrees_with_from_str`];
/// the identity carried through a generic `impl TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`
/// consumer at every variant is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstring_carries_through_generic_consumer`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on non-UTF-8 owned NUL-terminated
/// C-string input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstring_rejects_non_utf8_input`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on valid-UTF-8 non-canonical owned
/// NUL-terminated C-string input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_cstring_rejects_non_canonical_input`].
///
/// THEORY.md §V.4 typed primitives: the by-value owned-buffer
/// NUL-terminated C-string try-conversion surface is a typed-primitive
/// site on [`AdmissionTier`] itself (one `TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`
/// impl routing through the borrowed [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] parse
/// peer on [`std::ffi::CString::as_c_str`]), not a per-consumer
/// `AdmissionTier::try_from(c.as_c_str())` bridge at every downstream
/// site that types its parse contract as `impl TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`
/// rather than [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] or [`std::str::FromStr`].
/// THEORY.md §VI.1 generation over composition: the canonical-label
/// grammar is named at one site ([`AdmissionTier::as_str`]), inverted at
/// one site ([`<AdmissionTier as std::str::FromStr>::from_str`]), and
/// every parse surface — [`std::str::FromStr`], [`serde::Deserialize`],
/// [`TryFrom<&str>`], [`TryFrom<String>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, str>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<str>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<str>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&[u8]>`], [`TryFrom<Vec<u8>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::borrow::Cow<'_, [u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<std::sync::Arc<[u8]>>`], [`TryFrom<std::rc::Rc<[u8]>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::OsStr>`], [`TryFrom<std::ffi::OsString>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::path::Path>`], [`TryFrom<std::path::PathBuf>`],
/// [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`], this [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] —
/// reads through it.
impl TryFrom<std::ffi::CString> for AdmissionTier {
    type Error = anyhow::Error;

    fn try_from(c: std::ffi::CString) -> Result<Self, Self::Error> {
        <Self as std::convert::TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>>::try_from(c.as_c_str())
    }
}

/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>> for AdmissionTier`] routes through
/// [`std::boxed::Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::as_ref`] on the caller-supplied
/// shrunk-owned NUL-terminated C-string and the by-reference
/// NUL-terminated C-string parse peer [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`]
/// (which itself composes [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] with
/// [`TryFrom<&str>`] which itself delegates through
/// [`<AdmissionTier as std::str::FromStr>::from_str`]), so a downstream
/// consumer bound by `impl TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>` (a serde
/// container that opts into `#[serde(try_from = "Box<CStr>")]` on a
/// wrapper field, a [`std::ffi::CString::into_boxed_c_str`] shrunk-
/// buffer input at the NUL-terminated C-string frontier that trades
/// the resizable-buffer [`std::ffi::CString`] receiver footprint for
/// a single-allocation immutable [`Box<std::ffi::CStr>`], a
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr`] + [`std::ffi::CStr::to_owned`] +
/// [`std::ffi::CString::into_boxed_c_str`] compose that owns the
/// FFI-returned NUL-terminated buffer with the resizable-buffer
/// slack shed, a generic try-conversion helper
/// `fn parse<T: TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>>` that composes with
/// shrunk-owned NUL-terminated C-string inputs) recovers an
/// [`AdmissionTier`] value from a shrunk-owned canonical
/// NUL-terminated C-string label through the same one-oracle grammar
/// the sibling [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`], [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`],
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::OsStr>>`],
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::path::Path>>`], and (one frontier below)
/// [`TryFrom<Box<str>>`], [`TryFrom<Box<[u8]>>`] shrunk-owned parse
/// peers already read at neighboring OS-string / Path / UTF-8 /
/// byte-slice frontiers.
///
/// The two-stage strictness discipline (UTF-8 validity at the
/// NUL-terminated C-string decode frontier gated by
/// [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`], canonical-label grammar at the parse
/// frontier gated by [`FromStr`]) is inherited unchanged from the
/// by-reference [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] peer via
/// [`std::boxed::Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::as_ref`] which yields a
/// `&std::ffi::CStr` view of the boxed inner payload without moving
/// out or reallocating.
///
/// The impl body picks [`std::boxed::Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::as_ref`]
/// rather than an intermediate `Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::into` +
/// `TryFrom<CString>` restatement: the [`AsRef`] view yields a
/// borrowed `&std::ffi::CStr` window over the boxed heap allocation
/// without converting the shrunk-owned receiver into a resizable
/// [`std::ffi::CString`] first, so the receiver pays no reallocation
/// and no capacity-vs-length metadata rebuild on the fast path — the
/// borrow-then-drop discipline the sibling [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`]
/// peer above applies at the resizable-buffer axis, lifted to the
/// shrunk-owned axis via
/// [`std::boxed::Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::as_ref`].
///
/// Mid-trio peer of the shrunk-owned NUL-terminated C-string parse
/// trio at the admission-tier ladder:
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>`] for [`crate::retry::PerAttemptRegion`]
/// (commit 1076700) opened the trio at the first ordered typed sum;
/// the closing peer at the third ordered typed sum is
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>`] for [`crate::version::BumpLevel`] in
/// a follow-up commit, matching the [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`]
/// borrowed-view NUL-terminated C-string parse opening order
/// (8777e9f → 95ddf71 → 5073623) at the borrowed-view counterpart,
/// the [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] owned-buffer NUL-terminated
/// C-string parse opening order (e73daa7 → 77cd0dd → 20357c7) at the
/// owned-buffer counterpart, the [`TryFrom<Box<str>>`] UTF-8
/// shrunk-owned parse opening order at the UTF-8 sibling one frontier
/// below, the [`TryFrom<Box<[u8]>>`] byte-slice shrunk-owned parse
/// opening order at the byte-slice sibling two frontiers below, the
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::OsStr>>`] OS-string shrunk-owned parse
/// opening order at the OS-string sibling above, and the
/// [`TryFrom<Box<std::path::Path>>`] filesystem-path shrunk-owned
/// parse opening order (315c145 → 657434c → 336e453) at the
/// filesystem-path sibling.
///
/// The identity `AdmissionTier::try_from(
/// std::ffi::CString::new(tier.as_str()).unwrap().into_boxed_c_str()
/// ).unwrap() == tier` at every [`AdmissionTier::ALL`] variant is
/// pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_box_cstr_agrees_with_from_str`];
/// the identity carried through a generic
/// `impl TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>` consumer at every variant is
/// pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_box_cstr_carries_through_generic_consumer`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on non-UTF-8 shrunk-owned
/// NUL-terminated C-string input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_box_cstr_rejects_non_utf8_input`];
/// the strict-rejection contract on valid-UTF-8 non-canonical
/// shrunk-owned NUL-terminated C-string input is pinned by
/// [`tests::test_admission_tier_try_from_box_cstr_rejects_non_canonical_input`].
///
/// THEORY.md §V.4 typed primitives: the shrunk-owned NUL-terminated
/// C-string try-conversion parse surface is a typed-primitive site on
/// [`AdmissionTier`] itself (one `TryFrom<Box<std::ffi::CStr>>` impl
/// routing through [`std::boxed::Box::<std::ffi::CStr>::as_ref`] and
