    /// [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString> for AdmissionTier`] rejects
    /// non-UTF-8 owned NUL-terminated C-string sequences at the
    /// [`std::ffi::CStr::to_str`] decode frontier inherited through the
    /// by-reference [`TryFrom<&std::ffi::CStr>`] delegation. A
    /// [`std::ffi::CString`] may hold any byte sequence excluding
    /// interior NUL — an owned `getenv(3)` payload under a non-UTF-8
    /// locale, an owned C-emitted log frame under a foreign character
    /// set, an owned [`std::ffi::CStr::to_owned`] of a raw
    /// `*const c_char` from a legacy C library. Pins the
    /// encoding-strictness contract at the owned-buffer NUL-terminated
    /// C-string frontier's first strictness gate so a downstream
    /// consumer bound by [`TryFrom<std::ffi::CString>`] inherits the
    /// same UTF-8-only encoding discipline the by-reference peer offers,
    /// at ONE typed-primitive site rather than a per-consumer
    /// [`std::ffi::CString::into_string`] + [`str::parse`] restatement.
    /// Sibling of the by-reference NUL-terminated C-string pin
    /// [`test_admission_tier_try_from_cstr_rejects_non_utf8_input`] at
    /// the by-reference peer, the byte-slice-owned-buffer pin
